WEBVTT

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.470
Y-You're kidding me...

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.790
<b>The Iceblade <b>Sorcerer
</b>Shall <b>Rule </b>the <b>World</b></b>

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.020
<b>Episode 3
The Boy Who Became the World's Strongest Sorcerer Enjoys a Day Off</b>

00:01:57.980 --> 00:01:59.750
I'm so tired.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.990
My legs can't take this anymore...

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.010
An animal howl?

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:06.580
A monster?

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:09.230
But I've never seen anything 
like that before.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.620
<i>It's abnormally sturdy.</i>

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.530
What the hell is that thing?!

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:28.830
<i>Maybe just for a moment—</i>

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:36.580
Evi!

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:40.960
Elisa!

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:49.060
Ray!

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.360
Yeah!

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:11.130
What on earth is this monster?

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:13.190
That was incredible, Ray!

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:14.840
You split that monster clean open.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.040
Elisa.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.820
Are you all right?

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:23.820
I was so scared!

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.820
There, there.

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:25.930
You did well.

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:30.440
This was thanks to you.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.460
Hey, Al.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:43.730
That withered... I mean, White.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:46.180
Maybe he's actually legit?

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:49.370
Let's go.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:50.500
Hey, Al!

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.250
I'm not yet— Hey!

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.020
<i>Is this for real?</i>

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.940
<i>Ray was actually that strong?!</i>

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:06.550
And stamp!

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:08.860
And now we've got them all.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:10.150
We did it.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:12.910
I'm really sorry for getting 
in everyone's way.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.570
You really didn't.

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:18.820
A practical exercise in this forest was 
already pretty rough for students.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.850
On top of that, Evi and I 
train our bodies every day,

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:24.340
and we forced you to keep up with our pace.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.180
If anything, it's the two of us 
who should be apologizing.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:28.320
That's right.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:29.190
Sorry about that.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:30.040
Not at all.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.750
Thank you, everyone.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.960
Elisa, you're just too adorable.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.360
Ray, you didn't even flinch.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:39.640
No, this too—

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.640
That backwoods forest training, right?

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:42.770
Right.

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:48.820
Um, Amelia, that kind of tickles.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:49.380
Um...

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:58.160
And the top score for this 
practical exercise goes to...

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.470
Amelia Rose's group!

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.410
<i>Wow. Tough crowd.</i>

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.780
That's just like Lady Amelia!

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.360
Oh, so noble.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.810
Eww! Why is that withered next to her?!

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.170
So gross!

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.550
Really, he's disgusting!

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:20.710
I mean, they only won because of Amelia.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:21.790
Obviously.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:26.520
Otherwise someone like that wouldn't have a 
chance to stand in front of us aristocrats!

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:27.550
That's right!

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:31.610
They're not really cheering for us, huh?

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:33.110
Looks that way.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:37.310
I guess everybody's not 
happy to see me up here.

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:40.520
You don't need to let that bother you.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:41.930
She's right.

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:44.280
It doesn't change the fact that we got the best score.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.400
Withered...

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.530
Typical aristocrats.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.620
That is exactly what I mean.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:01.040
Amelia?

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.200
It's too soon, you know?

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:18.820
Not yet.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:21.500
Ugh, I know!

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:23.560
But it's been two months!

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:26.110
Three days is enough for a young boy
to become a totally new person!

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.520
And it's been twenty times that.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.570
Twenty times!

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:32.990
It looks like he's here.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.590
He is?

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:37.060
I will go get him.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:39.240
Please do.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.170
It's been a long time, Master Ray.

00:06:57.170 --> 00:06:58.770
It really has, Carla.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:03.020
Well, then. Lady Lydia is waiting for you.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:08.290
Excuse me.

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:10.810
Ray, is that you?

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:12.040
It's been a while.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:16.300
Have you grown?

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:18.950
I don't think so, Master.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.040
I see.

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:23.900
But I guess these days, 
I'm the one looking up at you.

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:25.260
It didn't used to be like that.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:27.700
Why don't you take a seat?

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:32.560
Are you doing well?

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:33.580
I am.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.050
But of course...

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.300
I see.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:38.910
So that's not there yet.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:42.370
I estimate that it'll take 
about five years or so.

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:43.570
Of course—

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:46.570
Using it is 
strictly forbidden, right?

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:48.530
That's right.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:52.150
However, if you ever feel like you absolutely need it,

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.940
you'll have to make the call.

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:58.660
After all, I did pass the mantle 
of "Iceblade Sorcerer" to you.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.720
Anyway, I called you here today

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:06.780
in regards to a rumor spreading 
among the sorcery researchers.

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:07.790
A rumor?

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:10.950
Is that really something you 
need to concern yourself with?

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:12.760
It is.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:16.550
I wouldn't bother myself 
with some petty rumor,

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.920
but Engram is another matter all together.

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:21.690
Engram?

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:24.760
Normally, when we talk 
about sorcery research,

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:26.340
we focus on sorcery itself,

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:29.070
that is to say, the code, right?

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.140
That is right.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:34.030
But what I'm researching 
is something different.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:36.630
So then, what are you researching?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:38.980
This.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:43.300
The head? No, the brain?

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:44.680
Yes.

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:48.880
You do know that sorcery 
begins in the brain, right?

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:49.720
I do.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:52.000
The frontal lobe of the brain

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.980
processes the internal information 
format according to code theory.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:57.800
It materializes when it comes into 
contact with the Prima materia.

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:01.930
That is the sorcery we utilize.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:02.920
Right.

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:06.880
By directing my attention to the brain,

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:08.930
I discovered the twofold code theory.

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:13.190
Announcing this has triggered 
an entirely new movement.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:17.010
Now, sorcery research and the brain 
are in a close relationship.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:18.120
I see.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:22.340
The part of the brain where memories
of sorcery are stored is...

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:23.550
Engram.

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:24.950
Exactly.

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:27.590
Researching the brain might lead 
to decoding sorcery itself,

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:32.290
actually, maybe even to the 
truth about our entire world.

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:34.600
Did you say that researching 
the brain and sorcery

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:36.180
will lead to decoding 
the truth of the world?

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.530
Isn't that an exciting prospect?

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:42.220
But then they always appear.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:46.340
The people who will do anything
to get what they want.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:47.730
What is that?

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:51.410
Instead of spending time to 
analyze the brain using sorcery,

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:54.480
these people cut open sorcerers' brains 
to rummage around inside.

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:59.600
They have no qualms about crossing the 
line that humanity must not cross.

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:02.350
Those delusional pieces of trash

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:05.960
call themselves "Eugenics".

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:07.510
Eugenics...

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:12.100
They wanted me to join them.

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:15.300
Those idiots believed I'd say yes.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:18.050
According to Carol,

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:22.060
they've begun contacting other 
prominent sorcerers, as well.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:26.460
If you do not have human dignity, 
you cannot advance sorcery.

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:28.550
Ray, you understand that, right?

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:31.060
Yes, I do.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:34.530
As I would expect from my star pupil.

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:42.720
It's so nice to take a walk in the forest!

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:44.840
Especially after a depressing 
talk like that.

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:48.700
Having you here like this brings 
back memories of our training days.

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:51.930
You mean the Ainsworth-style boot camp.

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:52.830
That brings back memories.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:56.620
That made even the military's elite give up,

00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:59.630
but you finished it as a child.

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:01.600
That was the only thing I was good at.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:05.930
Ray, you've made some friends, haven't you?

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:08.180
Yes.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:13.120
I've made some wonderful friends 
since entering the academy,

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:17.640
including a half-elf girl who 
absolutely loves your books.

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:23.740
I want you to bring them next time.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:26.440
Sure. I didn't think you'd be so excited.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:32.450
I mean, your smile was a lot stiffer 
before you entered the academy.

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:37.070
Of course I want to meet the people 
who have softened your smile.

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.090
Master...

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:45.660
It's almost June.

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:48.200
The Magic Chevalier will be starting soon.

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:51.430
That's the magic sword-fighting competition

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:53.850
held between the kingdom's three 
sorcery academies, right?

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:55.270
Yes.

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:58.110
Incidentally, I've won four times in a row.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.740
If you entered it, I'm sure you'd 
also be able to win four in a row.

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:03.700
I think I'd rather stay 
more in the background.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.900
Of course one reason is my recuperation,

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:08.990
but I also want to cheer on my friends.

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.630
Please do as you like.

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:12.570
After all...

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:14.850
Now that I am like this,

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:17.490
I no longer have the power to protect you.

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:18.730
That's not true.

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:21.250
Seeing you has reassured me, though.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.370
I'll pass this on to you.

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:27.510
I'm sure it will be of use to you someday.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.330
Thank you very much.

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:32.850
That's a version adapted 
specifically for a student.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.250
Really?

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:36.600
I figured it might come in handy.

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:38.250
You really are amazing.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:39.040
Again.

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:39.500
Huh?

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:40.390
Praise me again.

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:41.600
You really are amazing.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:43.170
That's so good. Again!

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:01.110
Oh, hey, Elisa.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:03.970
Good morning, Ray.

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:05.210
Good morning.

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:07.770
Are you going somewhere?

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:12.480
I was thinking I'd go visit the library and 
the bookstore in the Middle District today.

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:14.360
That sounds great.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:15.890
Do you mind if I come along?

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:22.960
I'm sorry I made you wait.

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:26.330
I hope this is all right.

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:28.410
I think you look really cute.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:30.800
Of course the pure white dress is nice,

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:32.900
but I especially like your hair like that.

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:35.450
It really accentuates your beauty.

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:37.240
Th-Thank you!

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:38.360
You're also...

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:40.580
Y-You're also looking great!

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:42.290
Thank you.

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:45.200
But anyway, why did you change clothes?

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:50.310
Well, since... we're going 
somewhere together.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:51.610
I see.

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:52.950
That makes sense.

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:54.860
You like to look nice, huh Elisa?

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:04.190
Thank you!

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:05.070
This is...

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:09.880
These are Dr. Ainsworth's early 
notes on her sorcery research.

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:11.420
You really like her, huh?

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:16.230
I do! I really like her revolutionary 
thinking that focuses on Engram.

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:22.040
This book's release kicked off an entirely 
new movement in sorcery research!

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:28.830
What are you reading?

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:30.270
It's a novel about love.

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:32.450
This is one of Luna Ether's works.

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:33.130
What?!

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:36.880
I-I'm sorry.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:38.550
Is that strange?

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:40.250
I guess so.

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:45.660
You can accurately feel the nuances of 
peoples' emotions when you read novels like these.

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:50.400
I feel like this author is 
especially good at depicting them.

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:52.790
Because I don't know these things,

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:54.400
I'm really drawn to learning about them.

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.150
I see.

00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:58.810
Well, I think that's really great, Ray.

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:06.550
What? I would've never expected 
to run into Ray at the library.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.810
And with another girl, too.

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:12.590
Why is approaching him so hard?

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:18.090
I just have to walk up with a 
smile and it won't be a problem.

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:20.520
That's what it said in that 
book I read the other day.

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:23.170
I see you're studying hard, Claris.

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:25.070
That's right!

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.540
I am of noble blood, after all.

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:31.100
I wasn't expecting to run into you here.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:31.680
What?

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.380
Well, that, that's just...

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:35.440
We're going to get some lunch now.

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:36.420
Would you like to join us?

00:15:37.630 --> 00:15:40.660
So what you mean is that you'd 
like for me to join you for lunch?

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:42.350
That's right.

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:47.210
I don't have a choice, do I?

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:49.820
I don't have a choice, 
so I'll do you a favor and join.

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:55.710
Let me introduce you.

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:58.010
This sweet angel is Elisa.

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:00.610
She's got an exceptionally beautiful heart,

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:02.990
excels at being considerate in subtle ways,

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:04.820
studies hard, and is vastly knowledgeable.

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:08.110
Uh, my name is Elisa Griffith.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:09.900
It's so nice to meet you!

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:13.490
And then this one-of-a-kind lady who loves

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:17.640
and is loved by these transcendentally 
wavy twintails is Claris.

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:21.330
She has the highest level of elegance, 
with which she expertly weaves

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:19.340
I—

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:21.080
<i>Um, that's...</i>

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.380
perfect sweetness into 
her otherwise cool demeanor.

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:26.460
My name is C-Claris Cleveland.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:29.190
I've never done this kind of thing before...

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:30.430
I mean...

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:32.690
Me, neither.

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:34.970
Me, neither.

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.260
Uh, the weather.

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:41.910
The weather is so nice today!

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:43.700
I-It really is!

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:45.570
This is so delicious.

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:48.080
It really is.

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:51.310
It's... nice to spend our day off together.

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:56.020
That is spot-on, um, Elisa.

00:16:56.020 --> 00:16:58.950
Thank you, Claris.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:02.960
Thank you for coming today, Ray.

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.620
See you in school.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:05.450
All right.

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:08.880
I can't believe your dad's also an Ainger.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:24.350
Ray!

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:27.100
What a surprise, running into you here.

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:30.420
The nobles had a gathering of sorts today.

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:32.820
It really gets so tiring.

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:35.460
Now that we're getting closer 
to the Magic Chevalier,

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:37.680
these meet and greets are only 
going to get more frequent.

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:42.160
Oh, I'm really sorry for venting like that.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.830
I don't mind.

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:46.680
I'm sure you need to get it 
off your chest sometimes.

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:47.830
Ray...

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:48.910
And then,

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:54.820
that formal outfit, which is distinctly different 
from our uniform, suits you incredibly well.

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:58.930
It really accentuates your beauty and wisdom.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:01.270
Thank you.

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:03.540
Speaking of, what have you been up to today?

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.230
Actually...

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:08.690
Hmm...

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:13.740
So you had lunch with Elisa and the 
daughter of the Cleveland family?

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:16.810
I'm sure you had a lot of fun.

00:18:16.810 --> 00:18:19.540
Yes, it was a lot of fun.

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:27.580
Hey! Will you go somewhere with me right now?

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:29.600
You have time, right?

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:31.260
I don't mind.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:39.060
Wow, that looks so feminine and beautiful!

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:42.940
So cute! My heart is tingling.

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:46.690
Very cool. So cool it's hot.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.780
You are a veritable Rose of Passion.

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:52.880
I've pricked my heart!

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:57.760
You know, I was thinking this before, too,

00:18:57.760 --> 00:19:00.820
but you certainly seem at ease with girls.

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:03.900
Really? I guess I never really 
thought about myself that way,

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:06.600
but I grew up in an environment 
with a lot of women.

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:08.450
Is that how that works?

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:10.920
Well, either way, that's...

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:12.870
I want wings.

00:19:22.110 --> 00:19:23.630
What's wrong, Amelia?

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:26.400
Amelia?

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:31.020
It's a... a... It's....

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:33.670
I'm so sorry!

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:40.870
This is too embarrassing.

00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:42.230
Amelia, are you all right?

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:43.730
I, uh, yes!

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:44.530
I'm sorry.

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:46.330
No, I'm the one who's sorry.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.620
I carelessly touched your bare skin.

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:52.630
Huh? Oh, that's not an issue.

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:53.580
I see.

00:19:59.810 --> 00:20:03.550
<i>Maybe I could show Ray who I really am, someday...</i>

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:08.070
I'm sorry to have summoned 
you so suddenly.

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:10.000
No, it's perfectly fine.

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:12.550
You don't have to be so formal.

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:14.740
This isn't the military.

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:15.870
I apologize.

00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:20.020
White, how are you finding 
life as a student?

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:22.580
I'm finding it extremely satisfying.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:24.160
Is that so?

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:26.690
Did something happen?

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:31.100
No. In all honesty, I was simply worried.

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:34.430
You're the first ordinary to enter 
the academy since its inception.

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:37.860
The noble-born students must 
be giving you a lot of grief.

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:39.820
I'm sorry.

00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:42.590
As aware of it as I am,

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:45.070
there is nothing I can 
presently do about it.

00:20:45.070 --> 00:20:47.330
It's not a problem at all.

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:50.810
I'm painfully aware of it myself.

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:55.560
Despite the fact that several years have passed 
since becoming a teacher at this academy,

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:58.360
I've still been trying to 
be a sorcery researcher.

00:20:59.350 --> 00:21:01.180
We get them every year.

00:21:01.180 --> 00:21:03.300
Whether it's due to relationships or grades,

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:05.220
they feel like they're not going to make it here,

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:07.790
and end up leaving the academy heartbroken.

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:13.560
All of them students who would have had 
the chance to become excellent sorcerers.

00:21:13.990 --> 00:21:16.440
I should have paid more attention.

00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:18.640
I should have approached them more.

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:21.610
I should have been a teacher who spent her life helping students

00:21:21.610 --> 00:21:24.640
instead of being some aloof researcher.

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:25.670
Professor Gray...

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:29.510
Sorry for being self-centered.

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:31.170
This is my ego showing.

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:36.330
But right now, I very strongly 
want to be your teacher.

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:39.580
You are my teacher, Professor Gray.

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:44.950
Does the teacher make the student, 
or does the student make the teacher?

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:49.280
At any rate, please come to me 
if you're having any problems.

00:21:49.650 --> 00:21:51.030
Thank you very much.

00:21:51.530 --> 00:21:53.170
I am very lucky.

00:21:53.990 --> 00:21:57.650
I am blessed with both friends and teachers.

00:21:58.560 --> 00:22:00.770
Thank you, Ray White.

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:10.230
Al hasn't come back to 
school since then, has he?

00:22:10.230 --> 00:22:11.810
I haven't seen him, either.

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:13.910
Where is he?

00:22:21.810 --> 00:22:27.940
Just you wait, Ray White!

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:55.030
<b>The Iceblade <b>Sorcerer
</b>Shall <b>Rule </b>the <b>World</b></b>

